From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Vishnefske <jvishnefske@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:40:58 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] std: io::copy kernel offload on linux-none

Use upstream's sys/io/kernel_copy/linux.rs (copy_file_range, sendfile
and splice, with its fallbacks) for linux_none too. linux_none.rs gives
it the three syscalls with libc's signatures and conventions (-1 and
errno) on linux_none_rt, and a cvt for that convention, in place of
libc's functions, sys::weak::syscall! and the Result-based sys::cvt.
